mmitted report — FR-2 (AC-2.1, 2.4, 2.5)."},{"line_number":42,"content":"- Every guard is pinned RED and mutation-verified — FR-6."},{"line_number":44,"content":"## Requirements"},{"line_number":45,"content":"- FR-1: surface-aware `_collected_path` — single derivation."},{"line_number":46,"content":"- FR-2: `h_mad_collect_report.py` with `COLLECT: OK|MISSING path=<docs path>"},{"line_number":47,"content":"  delivered=report-file|out|none [forced=1]` +"},{"line_number":48,"content":"  `[H-MAD] <feature> collect <verdict>` on every verdict and `[H-MAD] … collect"},{"line_number":49,"content":"  readback_failed` on a readback disagreement (Marker discipline), exit 0 on any verdict /"},{"line_number":52,"content":"- FR-3: gate refuses `TRANSPORT_RE` (`audit_` prefix, dot-free stem, `.report.md` suffix,"},{"line_number":54,"content":"  `_collected_path`) with exactly `GATE: INVALID must=0 should=0` + the `[H-MAD] <stem>"},{"line_number":55,"content":"  gate INVALID (transport file …)` marker (the feature slot carries the dot-free transport"},{"line_number":56,"content":"  stem verbatim — a transport name has no reliable feature grammar), exit 2; `<feature>.report.md` (Phase 7) still"},{"line_number":57,"content":"  scores; verdict preserved for every existing audit doc (AC-3.7, Backward compatibility)."},{"line_number":58,"content":"- FR-1 (AC-1.6): disjointness of the two grammars is a property test over adversarial"},{"line_number":61,"content":"- FR-4: `hmad-dispatch collect-report` wrapper verb."},{"line_number":62,"content":"- FR-5: SKILL.md codex-leg recipe (halt `<phase>:report_not_collected` emits its `[H-MAD]`"},{"line_number":64,"content":"- FR-6: tests for every AC including the incident replay (AC-2.9), operational errors"},{"line_number":65,"content":"  (AC-2.10) and readback (AC-2.12); mutation spec with 23 named-test mutations — every new"},{"line_number":67,"content":"  property (regex loosened / docs pattern de-dotted); wrapper wiring test for the verb in both directions (AC-4.1, AC-4.3);"},{"line_number":70,"content":"## Implementation Strategy"},{"line_number":74,"content":"cannot-judge carries no counts, exit 0 on any verdict, docs pinned bidirectionally); the"},{"line_number":81,"content":"(`TRANSPORT_RE` + the AC-1.6 / AC-3.5a grammar tests); (3) the CLI; **then the"},{"line_number":82,"content":"AC-2.9 tracer** — it needs (2)'s refusal for its step (i) and (3)'s CLI for step (ii), so it"},{"line_number":86,"content":"## Architecture Considerations"},{"line_number":92,"content":"  reports are `<feature>.report.md`; the cycle-2 rule (a `_cycle<N>[_tok]` stem) was wrong"},{"line_number":99,"content":"  pairs (AC-1.6) rather than by a production assert: the v1.3 draft put an assert in"},{"line_number":110,"content":"  one (grep: 0) — and its bytes keep their verdict at the docs path. AC-3.7 runs"},{"line_number":117,"content":"  readback that disagrees is an operational failure (exit 2, no `COLLECT:` line)."},{"line_number":118,"content":"- **A non-`OK` collect never reaches the gate.** `MISSING` and `CONFLICT` exit 0 (verdicts),"},{"line_number":125,"content":"- **Signal discipline.** `COLLECT: MISSING` and `CONFLICT` are verdicts, so they exit 0;"},{"line_number":126,"content":"  the teeth are in the gate (FR-3), not in the collector's exit code. `audit_cycle.gate()`"},{"line_number":130,"content":"  collector must treat that as already-collected (AC-2.8) rather than as a self-copy."},{"line_number":136,"content":"## Assumption verification (evidence, 2026-09-02)"},{"line_number":155,"content":"## Deliverables"},{"line_number":158,"content":"| `_collected_path(surface=None)` + `collect(surface=None)` | module change | FR-1 |"},{"line_number":159,"content":"| `_copy_collected_report` conflict-safe | module change | FR-2 (AC-2.5) |"},{"line_number":160,"content":"| `h_mad_collect_report.py` | CLI | FR-2 |"},{"line_number":161,"content":"| `TRANSPORT_RE` + `is_transport_path()` + refusal in the gate | module change | FR-3 |"},{"line_number":162,"content":"| `hmad-dispatch collect-report` | CLI verb | FR-4 |"},{"line_number":163,"content":"| SKILL.md codex-leg block, registry entry, step-9 sentence; orchestration-mode verb row | docs | FR-5 |"},{"line_number":164,"content":"| `tests/test_h_mad_collect_report.py` (incl. incident replay AC-2.9, operational errors AC-2.10), gate tests (AC-3.1–3.6), docs tests (AC-5.1–5.4) | tests | FR-6 |"},{"line_number":165,"content":"| wrapper wiring test: `collect-report` verb → script (severed route fails) | test | FR-4, FR-6 |"},{"line_number":166,"content":"| `tests/mutation-specs/collect_report.json` — 23 mutations, drop/force pairs per connection incl. fall-through paths and the grammar-disjointness property | mutation spec | FR-6 |"},{"line_number":167,"content":"| two-direction name corpus fixture asserted against `TRANSPORT_RE` and `_VERSION_RE`; verdict-preservation sweep over `docs/**/*.audit.v*.md` | tests | FR-3 (AC-3.5a, 3.7) |"},{"line_number":169,"content":"## Risks and Mitigation"},{"line_number":177,"content":"| Transport grammar drifts from what gets staged (a future naming change silently un-guards) | transport files score again | one grammar (`TRANSPORT_RE`), one corpus fixture in both directions, the wrapper's staged `--report-file` asserted against it under the stub harness, the 6.6 literal asserted too (AC-3.5a) |"},{"line_number":178,"content":"| `CONFLICT` followed by a hand-run gate scores stale bytes | wrong verdict on a preserved old report | recipe halt on non-`OK` (AC-5.3 docs test); `--force` is the only overwrite path |"},{"line_number":182,"content":"## Convention Prerequisites"},{"line_number":191,"content":"## Success Criteria"},{"line_number":192,"content":"- All 40 unique ACs in the spec pass automated tests (AC-2.9's hand replay is recorded, its suite half asserted)."},{"line_number":193,"content":"- `MUTATION: ALL_CAUGHT` on `collect_report.json` (25 mutations, every connection dropped"},{"line_number":195,"content":"- Incident replay (AC-2.9) passes in the suite and once by hand against a real `/tmp`"},{"line_number":202,"content":"## Out-of-Scope (confirmed from spec)"},{"line_number":205,"content":"- Deleting `/tmp` transport files after collection (only the AC-2.8 docs-path marker)."},{"line_number":208,"content":"## Next Steps"},{"line_number":209,"content":"Operator approves v1.0 → Phase 3 audit cycle (agy via `audit-cycle --passes 1` + codex via"},{"line_number":212,"content":"## Version History"},{"line_number":213,"content":"- v1.0: Initial plan draft."},{"line_number":216,"content":"- v1.3: Audit v3 fixes from .plan.audit.v3.p1.md (agy: [H-MAD] markers named in Requirements) + .v3.codex.md (TRANSPORT_RE stem is dot-free so the grammars are disjoint by construction; _collected_path asserts it, AC-1.6, 17 mutations; the CLI does not import the regex)."},{"line_number":217,"content":"- v1.4: Audit v4 fixes from .plan.audit.v4.codex.md (agy v4 clean, low-evidence) — work order reordered so the gate refusal (task 2) precedes the CLI (task 3) and the AC-2.9 tracer runs after task 3, the first point at which both its steps can pass."},{"line_number":218,"content":"- v1.5: Audit v6 fixes from .plan.audit.v6.codex.md (agy v6 clean, low-evidence) — AC-1.6 is a grammar-disjointness property test, not an unreachable production assert; forced=1 in the FR-2 contract line; Scope wording distinguishes the CLI's no-clobber default from audit-cycle's unchanged overwrite."},{"line_number":220,"content":"- v1.7: Count sweep from 5b-audit v2 (codex): 23 mutations (exit-only/token-only mutants per guard). No plan decision changed."},{"line_number":222,"content":"- v1.9: Count sweep from 5b-audit v8 (codex): e′ restored on the observable bad-project-root path → 23 mutations. No plan decision changed."},{"line_number":223,"content":"- v1.10: Wording sweep from 5b-audit v10: the transport refusal marker's feature slot is the stem (matches design/impl-plan). No plan decision changed."},{"line_number":224,"content":"- v1.11: AC-2.9h hand replay 2026-09-02 survivor=/tmp/audit_nlmpin_plan_cycle8_codex.report.md (scratch root, not HemaSuite): gate(RP)=GATE: INVALID must=0 should=0 rc=2 · collect=COLLECT: OK path=<R>/docs/01-plan/features/nlm-cli-version-pin.plan.audit.v8.codex.md delivered=report-file · cmp=identical · gate(docs)=GATE: FAIL must=3 should=1 rc=0"}]}]},"locations":[]}
